1. Validation rules

I propose these become permanent MOS invariants.

RI-001 — Every persistent object has an identity

Every first-class persistent object must have:

UUID
created_at

and, where mutable:

updated_at
version
status
RI-002 — Events are immutable

Events may be:

created
read
linked
projected

but never:

updated
deleted
RI-003 — Foreign keys use RESTRICT by default

This is extremely important.

We don't want:

Entity
   ↓
Fact
   ↓
Evidence

and then deleting the entity automatically destroying the provenance chain.

Therefore MOS defaults to:

ON DELETE RESTRICT

not:

ON DELETE CASCADE

Exceptions must be explicitly justified.

RI-004 — Provenance cannot disappear

A fact without provenance is not a valid MOS fact.

Conceptually:

FACT
 │
 ├── source
 ├── evidence
 └── originating event

must remain reconstructable.

RI-005 — Graph is a projection

This is one of the most important decisions.

Fact
  ↓
Graph edge

not:

Graph edge
  ↓
Fact

The graph must never become the authoritative source of knowledge.

RI-006 — Embeddings are projections

Similarly:

Fact
Episode
Document
Skill
...
   ↓
Embedding

An embedding can disappear and be regenerated.

Therefore:

Losing an embedding must never mean losing knowledge.

