29. The most important distinction: authoritative vs projected

We should formally divide MOS objects into two classes.

Authoritative
Events
Entities
Sources
Evidence
Assertions
Facts
Fact Versions
Goals
Plans
Tasks
Procedures
Execution records

These contain actual MOS state.

Derived / projected
Graph
Embeddings
Summaries
Search indexes
Rerankings
Semantic cache

These can always be regenerated.

That gives us a powerful invariant:

If every authoritative object survives, MOS can reconstruct its derived state.

That is one of the strongest properties we can give the system.

