What I recommend we do next

Do not run another migration yet.

The correct next sequence is:

Apply RI-FIX-001 → RI-FIX-014 to the canonical Storage Specification.
Re-run the relational integrity validation.
Perform a lifecycle/state-machine validation — especially facts, versions, procedures, plans, tasks, executions and projections.
Perform a cross-spec validation against:
MOS Core Spec
Storage Spec
API Spec
Worker Spec
Network Spec
Freeze MOS Storage v0.1.0.
Only then generate the final PostgreSQL migrations.
Build schema-level automated tests that make these invariants executable.

That way, the migration you already started becomes a draft implementation, rather than something we have to treat as immutable architecture. The important thing is that we now have a precise list of where it needs to evolve before we call the storage layer stable.
